  "review": [
    "The former MOV body installed a catalog 404 and never opened the recording. The new Router test opens it before create release and waits for the same-thread catalog request. The error arm is retained in the replay.",
    "The model control contrasts a genuinely empty response with managed Auto. The frozen body assumed no available model. The isolated run-models API establishes the supported catalog independently of the page fixture.",
    "The original Stripe fixture manufactured no-auth Stripe. The current directed entry posts the selected account credential before its chat callback. This does not establish the original no-auth premise.",
    "The old snapshot and indicators bodies called a private bridge and worker driver. The snapshot error is now received on the registered Router readiness promise. The same promise fulfills for the indicators failure.",
    "For the worker, cursor and IndexedDB cases the comparisons retain the original return-shape and transaction requirements. External telemetry records only public operation metadata; the native program has no access to the app store or the worker response channel.",
    "The signed-object fixture validates expiry and HMAC on a separate loopback server. Window aliases are supplied to the synthetic identity provider and external telemetry SDK. The Gmail replay uses stock Chromium, the real local API and isolated PostgreSQL.",
    "The main merge retains reconstructed Finance and Chat owners. Its new member-wide approval actions and free workspace purchases are regression coverage, separate from this batch\u2019s frozen dispositions."
  ]
